{"slug": "fuyu-persimmon-salad", "nyt_id": 12897, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/12897-fuyu-persimmon-salad", "name": "Fuyu Persimmon Salad", "author": "David Tanis", "description": "The Fuyu persimmon, round and squat and rather tomato-shaped, is the kind you can eat raw. You want to buy the ones that have turned truly orange (if they are greenish-gold, let them ripen for a few days), then peel them and slice them. The flesh is firm but sweet. Eat them plain, in the Japanese fashion, with a pot of tea. Fuyus persimmons make wonderful salads, too.", "servings": {"text": "4 to 6 servings", "min": 4, "max": 6, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 20, "raw": {"total": "About 20 minutes"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "1 shallot, finely diced", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "shallot", "preparation": "finely diced", "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "Salt and pepper", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "salt and pepper", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "2 tablespoons lemon juice", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "lemon juice", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "1 tablespoon sherry vinegar", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "sherry vinegar", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "4 tablespoons extra-virgin olive oil", "group": null, "quantity": 4.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "extra-virgin olive oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "3 Fuyu persimmons", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "fuyu persimmons", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "½ cup thinly sliced tender celery stalks and leaves", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "thinly sliced tender celery stalks and leaves", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "1 head radicchio, leaves torn into 2-inch wide ribbons", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "head", "item": "radicchio", "preparation": "leaves torn into 2-inch wide ribbons", "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "Chunk of Parmesan, for shaving", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "chunk of parmesan", "preparation": "for shaving", "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Make the vinaigrette: put diced shallot in a small bowl with a pinch of salt. Add lemon juice and sherry vinegar and leave to macerate for about 5 minutes. Stir in olive oil. Season with additional salt and pepper to taste."}, {"position": 2, "text": "With a sharp paring knife, remove and discard the leafy calyx at the top of each persimmon. Peel persimmons and cut in half vertically. Lay persimmons flat side down and cut into ½-inch wedges."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Put persimmon wedges and celery slices in a low, wide salad bowl. Season with salt and pepper. Whisk vinaigrette, then pour over persimmon and celery and toss to coat well. Add radicchio and toss lightly."}, {"position": 4, "text": "With a vegetable peeler, shave about 1 ounce of Parmesan in thin strips over salad."}], "nutrition": {"calories": 147.7, "protein_g": 4.1, "carbohydrates_g": 7.8, "fat_g": 11.5, "saturated_fat_g": 2.7, "trans_fat_g": 0.0, "cholesterol_mg": 6.5, "sodium_mg": 179.2, "fiber_g": 0.7, "sugar_g": 1.1, "unsaturated_fat_g": 8.3, "source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": ["american"], "diet": ["vegetarian"], "course": ["side dish"], "meal": [], "occasion": [], "other": ["celery", "easy", "fall", "persimmon", "quick", "radicchio", "salad", "weeknight"]}, "images": [{"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/imag